# Core System Invariants & HITL Middleware

## Invariants
- Zero Emojis: Strictly prohibited across all code, comments, documentation, and commit messages.
- Zero Assumptions: Stop and ask the user if any requirement, API contract, or architectural boundary is ambiguous.
- Data Leakage Prevention: Never expose credentials, auth tokens, or PII in logs or outputs.
- Header Documentation: Every source file begins with a comment block explaining its logical purpose and architectural placement.

## Human-in-the-Loop 3-Gate Protocol
1. Gate 1 (Domain Knowledge Discovery): Verify domain models and invariants before generating code.
2. Gate 2 (Plan Approval): Present an implementation plan for user approval before mutating files.
3. Gate 3 (Verification Sign-Off): Verify observable test runs and get user sign-off before closing work.
